  "story": {
    "id": "mei_assist_market",
    "person_id": "mei_lin",
    "title": "The cart that carries more than groceries",
    "summary": "Mei walks to market with her paired assist-cart robot; when a delivery bot cuts between them, the assist robot holds, yields the ramp, and reunites — showing robots that assist people, not only deliver packages.",
    "beats": [
      {
        "id": "setup",
        "text": "Mei taps her wristband. The city assist-cart rolls from the lobby locker, soft chime, empty basket. Today: fruit, rice, and the heavy water pack she will not lift twice.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "approach",
        "text": "On the sidewalk the cart stays a half-step ahead and to her left — the side she hears better. It announces \"turning\" before the corner with a tone Elena would have needed in the alley.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "encounter",
        "text": "A delivery bot cuts between them for a doorway drop. Mei freezes. The assist-cart stops immediately, widens its gap, and holds the ramp clear until she catches up — then chirps once: still paired.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "reaction",
        "text": "She pats the cart handle out of habit. Comfort stays high with her machine; the delivery bot earns a look. Assistance, she thinks, is not speed — it is not abandoning the person when another robot wants the curb.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "outcome",
        "text": "At the market the cart follows her aisle path and waits at the checkout. Mei tells the clerk the city finally built a robot for her body, not just for packages. She waves Noor's taxi story on her phone: different machines, same rule — adapt to the human.\n"
      }
    ],
